- [ ] "Open with Cockpit" from the OS file manager <!-- id: k6 labels: feature -->
      Document-type association (Info.plist on macOS, extension registration on Windows/Linux) plus the open-file handler: opens a lightweight file window without showing the full workspace.

- [ ] Document the new features on the Cockpit page of the site <!-- id: k2 labels: docs -->
      `../site`: .env.cockpit, Restart tab, Neovim, workspace CLI, remote hosts, Gallery documents, Database panel and everything else that shipped since the page was last updated.

- [ ] Multi-window: detach a file tab into its own window <!-- id: k10 labels: feature -->
      Viewer, .kanban, .html, .http, .dbq and diff tabs carry only a path and a mode, so a second window can rebuild them. Each Flutter window is a separate engine/isolate: state crosses only as messages. This slice gives most of the two-monitor value.


