## Review

## Done

- [x] Decide: macOS sandbox stays off? <!-- labels: decision -->
      Decided 2026-09-12: sandbox stays OFF on desktop, by design. Cockpit spawns shells, git, ssh, pi and LSP servers, reads any project folder and owns a Unix socket; none of that fits the App Sandbox. Sandbox is only required for the Mac App Store, which is out of scope. Hardened Runtime, notarization and TCC prompts stay. Mobile clients (iOS/Android) are sandboxed by the platform and do not run local shells. Follow-up: review whether cs.disable-library-validation is still needed in Release.entitlements.

- [x] Keyboard shortcut to switch between workspaces <!-- labels: feature -->
      Done 2026-09-12: Cmd+Shift+N (previous) and Cmd+Shift+M (next), Ctrl+Shift on Windows/Linux, in the View menu next to Select Tab. Cycles the rail in visual order (root then its worktrees), wraps around, skips the Cockpit system terminal. No digit shortcuts on purpose: worktrees make positions unstable.

- [x] Explicit approval for .env.cockpit in a freshly cloned repo <!-- labels: security -->
      Done 2026-09-12, downscoped: no trust dialog (a cloned repo already runs its own scripts and hooks). Instead: (1) keys that change who runs what are never injected (PATH, SHELL, HOME, ZDOTDIR, BASH_ENV, ENV, PROMPT_COMMAND, IFS, LD_* and DYLD_*); (2) when the .env.cockpit is tracked by git (it came with the repository) new terminals print a yellow notice listing the injected key names, never values.

- [x] Drag-and-drop a file into the terminal steals the tab focus <!-- labels: bug -->
      Fixed 2026-09-12: a native drop generates no pointer event and the drag from Finder/Explorer leaves the Cockpit window non-key, so no focus path ran. After injecting the paths the terminal now brings the window to front, focuses its pane in the VM and re-requests the terminal focus node post-frame. Needs a manual check with a real drop after the next release.

- [x] Green test suite on main <!-- labels: hygiene -->
      Done 2026-09-12: 1412 passing, 0 failing. The two hamburger-menu tests still described the old nested submenus (the menu was flattened on purpose in 64b7e36d) and were rewritten for the flat sections. The two xterm IME tests failed because flutter_test reports Android, where the terminal only opens its text-input connection after a tap (317e6a94); they now pin the desktop platform during the initial pump. No production code changed.

- [x] Analyzer noise in tool/ and packages/ <!-- labels: hygiene -->
      Done 2026-09-12: `flutter analyze` reports zero issues. packages/** and tool/wave*/** are excluded from the root analysis (own pubspec/context; run `dart analyze` inside each package). The 56 real lints in lib/ were fixed: initializing formals, curly braces, six missing awaits inside try blocks, the deprecated gpt_markdown highlightBuilder (now inlineCodeBuilder returning a span), a private render type in a public API, an unused test class and an ambiguous import in the e2e script.

- [x] Redact injected secrets in terminal output <!-- labels: security -->
      Done 2026-09-12: values from .env.cockpit (8+ chars) are replaced by *** before the output reaches the emulator, so screen, saved scrollback and `cockpit read-tab` are covered at once. Chunk-safe: only the shortest tail that could still be the start of a secret is held back, so latency stays zero in practice. ~170 MiB/s on yes-like output. Out of scope by decision: values encoded (base64) or split by ANSI escapes, and reading the file itself.

- [x] Mermaid diagrams <!-- labels: feature -->
      Done 2026-09-12: ```mermaid fences render as SVG in the markdown preview (Mermaid 11 bundled as an asset, no network, fits the nonce CSP). Rendered before the DOM diff with a per-source cache, so editing keeps scroll and only the changed diagram re-renders; dark/light follows the app theme; invalid diagrams show the source plus the error. Verified in headless Chrome under the real CSP. Not covered: the Linux native (non-webview) preview, and .html tabs, which keep JavaScript disabled by design (separate decision if the HTML view should run scripts).

- [x] .env.cockpit on remote workspaces <!-- labels: feature -->
      Done 2026-09-12: the remote terminal gateway reads <root>/.env.cockpit (and each multi-root root) on the host via fs.read right before spawning, merges it under the Cockpit env, and the tab's secret redaction is updated once the values arrive. No cockpit-server change and no protocol change. Blocked keys apply the same way. Not covered: the git-tracked notice (needs a remote `git ls-files`), left out on purpose.

- [x] Kanban: card dependencies (blocked by) <!-- labels: feature -->
      Done 2026-09-12: `blockedBy: k1, k2` in the card comment (by id, either order with labels). Card footer replaced the note preview: `#id`, comment icon with count, and "blocked by N" (pending blockers only, tooltip lists them) or "blocks N". Detail panel has a Blocked by row with chips (struck through when done, unknown ids marked) and a searchable card picker. Filter popover gained Blocked/Ready toggles. Blockers get an id when linked; a card never blocks itself. Not done: the warning when moving a blocked card to the last column.

